  "claim": "The travel hub, which is south of Tafuna, American Samoa, and Hoonah Airport both are on American territory.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Pago Pago International Airport. Sentence: Pago Pago International Airport (IATA: PPG, ICAO: NSTU, FAA LID: PPG) , also known as Tafuna Airport, is a public airport located 7 miles (11.3 km) southwest of the central business district of Pago Pago, in the village and plains of Tafuna on the island of Tutuila in American Samoa, an unincorporated territory of the United States.\nPage: Hoonah Airport. Sentence: Hoonah Airport (IATA: HNH, ICAO: PAOH, FAA LID: HNH) is a state-owned public-use airport located one nautical mile (2 km) southeast of the central business district of Hoonah, Alaska.\nPage: Tafuna, American Samoa. Sentence: It is located on a peninsula a mile north of Pago Pago International Airport and one mile south of Nu'uuli, American Samoa.",
