        "original_id": "1fff3bc6-c7b6-5f28-ab31-af60b26de9a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pago Pago International Airport, Hoonah Airport, Tafuna, Pago Pago, Hoonah, Tutuila, American Samoa, Alaska, Nu'uuli\n- Products: IATA codes, ICAO codes, FAA LIDs\n- Topics: airport location, geographic proximity\n\nFacts:\n- Pago Pago International Airport is also known as Tafuna Airport.\n- Pago Pago International Airport has the codes IATA PPG, ICAO NSTU, and FAA LID PPG.\n- Pago Pago International Airport is a public airport located 7 miles southwest of the central business district of Pago Pago in Tafuna on Tutuila in American Samoa.\n- Hoonah Airport has the codes IATA HNH, ICAO PAOH, and FAA LID HNH.\n- Hoonah Airport is a state-owned public-use airport located 1 nautical mile southeast of the central business district of Hoonah, Alaska.\n- Tafuna, American Samoa, is located on a peninsula 1 mile north of Pago Pago International Airport and 1 mile south of Nu'uuli, American Samoa.",
